es.toml's 132 changed / 30 added / 3 removed rows (OI-64, OI-65, OI-67, WI-522, WI-528, WI-530, WI-531, WI-533, WI-534, WI-553), components.toml's 1 changed row (WI-520) and one external.toml comment correction — and is resealed at the successor's approval commit, or does the owner REVIEW that diff first (git diff 6d3d9db4 551d1b2c -- docs/archive/last_approved/docs/requirements/) and amend any rejected row LIVE, which returns it to the re-attestation brief, before the reseal? (A byte-level restore of the old snapshot is unavailable: the mirror invariant reds a snapshot that is not a copy of live at its writing commit.)\"\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tIN SCOPE — four rows and one baseline question.\n43\t\n44\t**The rows.** `LLR-203`, `LLR-204` (`Approved` on trunk) and `TC-199`, `TC-200`\n45\t(`Drafted` on trunk, `verifies = [\"LLR-203\"]` / `[\"LLR-204\"]`, `Expected` scoped\n46\tto the LLR arm). Draw the ONE clean cross-family reviewer round the WI-508 lane\n47\tnever landed — the \"fresh reviewer round on a refreshed tree\" its own handback\n48\treport lists under *Not delivered* — on CURRENT trunk, confirming the four rows\n49\tstand in their reviewed state. **The `580df781` `Drafted` -> `Approved` flips of\n50\t`LLR-203`/`LLR-204` are KEPT by the WI-568 adjudication**: that is a named keep\n51\tdecision, not a defaulted one — the flip was loop-permitted under\n52\t`human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Needs\"` and the rows are byte-identical to the\n53\tround-010-approved tree (`b8d57e9f`), so the successor CONFIRMS them and does not\n54\tre-litigate the flip. `TC-199`/`TC-200` STAY `Drafted`; do not approve them here\n55\t(their `verifies` drift is normal on an unapproved row).\n56\t\n57\t**The baseline.** Apply the owner's ruling on the `open_item` above, and only\n58\tafter it lands (the mint parks this row `waiting:open-item-pending`):\n59\t- ruling **\"stand\"** -> regenerate `docs/archive/last_approved/` with `python\n60\t  project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py --root 