or the off-spine registries where it read 132 before\n88\t  the merge. Nothing on the spine (LLR/TC) moves under either answer.\n89\t- *Options.* **STAND** — accept the bytes as the baseline; this row regenerates\n90\t  the snapshot with `intake.py snapshot` at its own approval commit, which\n91\t  re-seals the same content. **REVIEW-THEN-STAND** — the owner reads the diff\n92\t  above; any row they reject is amended live, which returns it to the brief\n93\t  through the ordinary path; the reseal follows that act. A byte-level RESTORE\n94\t  is unavailable by construction (the mirror invariant, above).\n95\t- *Recommendation.* **REVIEW-THEN-STAND.** STAND is within authority\n96\t  (`DevStg-Needs` leaves the Arch and Boundary rungs loop-approvable), but the\n97\t  132 rows entered the baseline as a side effect of a `partial` lane's\n98\t  handback merge, not as an approval act, and were never shown to anyone as a\n99\t  batch. Reading the diff once costs an hour; STAND without it accepts rows\n100\t  unseen.\n101\t- *Reversal cost.* STAND then review later: any row can still be amended live\n102\t  at any time and re-enters the brief — nothing is lost, only the batch view.\n103\t  REVIEW-THEN-STAND: the amendments are ordinary edits; the reseal is one\n104\t  `intake.py snapshot` commit.\n105\t\n106\t**Inherited ruling.** This row inherits `OI-72`'s `SR-163` ruling (owned and\n107\tdischarged by the re-scoped `WI-543`); do not re-open the `SR-163` shape.\n108\t\n109\t**Routed here rather than dropped** — the two `BLOCKER`s of\n110\t`docs/reviews/wi508-architectural-remap/010-REVIEW-A-5175065.md`, which the\n111\tWI-508 close left on no queue and which target files that are on trunk:\n112\t1. `docs/plans/2026-08-25-blind-minimal-map-brief.md:3` — the anti-post-hoc\n113\t   condition is uncovered: brief and both agent returns first appear together in\n114\t   `64e9bf2a`, so nothing immutably fixes the question before the answers exist.\n115\t2. `docs/plans/2026-08-25-