(codex-effort-dial-and-config-inheritance.md) — no --effort flag; pin via `-c model_reasoning_effort=` in cmd_template; unpinned rows inherit ~/.codex/config.toml (xhigh here); all three rows pinned medium 2026-09-01\n- [Supervised loop 2026-09-01 evening lessons](supervised-loop-2026-09-01-evening-lessons.md) — hand-compiled rollup stops every lane; pre-snapshot lanes cannot refresh (merge trunk in first); adjudication C6 loop -> stop loop, close via handback.close_adjudication; hostile rounds catch the supervisor too\n- [venv symlink trap 2026-09-02](venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02.md) — a lane .venv symlink left the repo .venv self-linked (ELOOP) mid-intake; rebuild venv from requirements-dev.txt, re-run intake_after_merge with the merge scope\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - [Commit often; push is the only gate](commit-often-push-is-the-only-gate.md) — owner wants frequent commits; `push = \"human\"` governs push alone, never commit — stop leaving work uncommitted"," - [Owner commit identity](owner-commit-identity.md) — canonical git identity is diytechy <78943505+diytechy@users.noreply.github.com>, set repo-local in ai-template; kit never sets identity so loop commits inherit ambient config"," - [status.md forward-only sharp edge](status-md-forward-only-sharp-edge.md) — scrub every done-WI-id token from status.md on close; WARN at commit bar but ERROR at G3 (+ hard test)","-- [Worker-lane close ritual traps](worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md) — Deliverable must stay EMPTY until the close commit (R-A rejects it); the docs/stage and wi_convert reds are trunk's or pre-existing, not yours; the close drains active/, so re-verify gating claims at the final tip","+- [Worker-lane close ritual traps](worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md) — Deliverable must stay EMPTY until the close commit (R-A rejects it); the docs/stage red is CAUSED-but-benign (bisect the node at the base before calling ANY red inherited) and wi_convert's is pre-existing; the close drains active/, so re-verify gating claims at the final tip","+- [Stale NOT-DISCHARGED clauses on Approved spine rows](stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows.md) — a row asserting \"no check does X\" silently becomes false when a later WI ships X; nothing detects it, so re-drive every negative claim"," - [Module-size ratchet phantom overage](module-size-ratchet-phantom-overage.md) — SLOC ignores docstrings/comments, so an extraction's overage is usually ruff-format expansion; compact it before taking a reviewed bump"," - [Re-derive, don't re-run, measured claims](rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims.md) — a derived count equal to a column's value counts is that column restated; verify by an independent route + one named instance"," - [OpenAI adversarial reviews via codex](openai-adversarial-reviews-via-codex.md) — sol/terra at medium effort via codex CLI; hostile brief; author re-verifies findings"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeeaY2Zkn7WoR97BAbxkG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rr3ju2st55vS5b85vUaUJ9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows.md","content":"---\nname: stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows\ndescription: \"An Approved spine row's NOT-DISCHARGED paragraph asserts a NEGATIVE that a later WI silently falsifies — no check detects it, so a review must re-drive every such claim\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nMeasured on WI-569, 2026-09-02, reviewing `LLR-203`/`LLR-204` (SR-163).\n\nThis repo's spine-authoring convention has a design row record what it does NOT\ndischarge — \"no cell joins an inventoried file to a requirement id … no check\nresolves\", \"every arm walks the DESTINATIONS the inventory declares, never the\nshipped tree\", \"the grammar and the dial are what the parent's join would ride;\nneither runs for it today\". The convention is good: it stops a row reading as\nthough the obligation were finished.\n\n**The failure mode: a later WI delivers exactly the mechanism the clause denies,\nand nothing notices.** WI-543 shipped the file-to-requirement join, an\nindependent physical-tree universe and a four-class warn-to-gate checker. Three\nof LLR-203's assertions and one of LLR-204's became false, on an `Approved` row,\non trunk, for days — while `trace.py --strict-integrity` read `integrity=0` and\nthe full suite was green.\n\n**Why nothing catches it.** Every mechanized check on the spine is structural —\nids resolve, symbols exist, statuses ladder, snapshots mirror. A *negative*\nprose claim has no referent to resolve: \"no check resolves X\" names nothing that\ncan go missing. The `code_symbol`/`module` cells still pointed at real symbols,\nso the row looked healthy from every angle a checker has.\n\n**How to apply.**\n- Reviewing a spine row = checking each cell against the tree TODAY, not\n  against the tree at approval. Treat a NOT-DISCHARGED paragraph as the highest-\n  risk part of the row, not boilerplate to skim.\n- Verify a negative by hunting the mechanism it denies and DRIVING it — a\n  one-line CLI run or an in-process call beats any amount of reading. Here:\n  `gen_arch_map.py --mapping-purpose --root .` and calling\n  `bootstrap.delivery_inventory()` settled three clauses in two commands.\n- Put this in the reviewer's brief explicitly (\"a row that says no check\n  resolves X is FALSE if some check now resolves X; verify by looking for the\n  mechanism, not by taking the sentence at its word\"). A cross-family reviewer\n  given that instruction found the same three independently.\n\n**Repairing it is a worker lane's job, and the machinery agrees.**\n`acceptance_record.lane_approval_refusal` says in as many words that \"a\nDE-APPROVAL IS NOT AN ACT, and neither is an amendment to an approved row\" — a\nlane amends cell text on any spine row including Approved ones, leaves `Status`\nalone, and `intake` mints an amendment adjudication at the merge that judges it.\nConfirm the handoff really fires rather than assuming:\n`acceptance_record.staged_spine_amendments(root, base, head)` must list the rows.\n\n**Split fact from design.** Correcting a false sentence is fact repair and is\nthe lane's. Deciding which row OWNS a newly delivered mechanism, whether a\n`code_symbol` widens, or where a TC's evidence re-binds needs the whole chain —\nleave it, and state it as the row's new NOT-DISCHARGED gap so the adjudication\nreads the finding in the cell where it will look.\n\nRelated: [[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]],\n[[rules-omit-sn-tier-and-need-detectors]],\n[[openai-adversarial-reviews-via-codex]], [[worker-lane-close-ritual-traps]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":224662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f485ca-7d86-46c9-85e6-54376a8c7e94","uuid":"36f408c8-0a3f-4130-9524-f2801b9a0092","request_id":"req_011CeeaXzVyqxLKT5EC5YASb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rr3ju2st55vS5b85vUaUJ9","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f485ca-7d86-46c9-85e6-54376a8c7e94","uuid":"94818aa3-d30e-4bf1-ae92-1d3c2b78c945","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:03:03.513Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows.md","content":"---\nname: stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows\ndescription: \"An Approved spine row's NOT-DISCHARGED paragraph asserts a NEGATIVE that a later WI silently falsifies — no check detects it, so a review must re-drive every such claim\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 84f485ca-7d86-46c9-85e6-54376a8c7e94\n---\n\nMeasured on WI-569, 2026-09-02, reviewing `LLR-203`/`LLR-204` (SR-163).\n\nThis repo's spine-authoring convention has a design row record what it does NOT\ndischarge — \"no cell joins an inventoried file to a requirement id … no check\nresolves\", \"every arm walks the DESTINATIONS the inventory declares, never the\nshipped tree\", \"the grammar and the dial are what the parent's join would ride;\nneither runs for it today\". The convention is good: it stops a row reading as\nthough the obligation were finished.\n\n**The failure mode: a later WI delivers exactly the mechanism the clause denies,\nand nothing notices.** WI-543 shipped the file-to-requirement join, an\nindependent physical-tree universe and a four-class warn-to-gate checker. Three\nof LLR-203's assertions and one of LLR-204's became false, on an `Approved` row,\non trunk, for days — while `trace.py --strict-integrity` read `integrity=0` and\nthe full suite