he row's new NOT-DISCHARGED gap so the adjudication\nreads the finding in the cell where it will look.\n\nRelated: [[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]],\n[[rules-omit-sn-tier-and-need-detectors]],\n[[openai-adversarial-reviews-via-codex]], [[worker-lane-close-ritual-traps]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeeaZdqaSU68CjGMSBWjW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-569 is closed on `wi-569-wi-508-spine-reseal-one-clean`, five commits, final one carrying `WI: WI-569`.\n\n## What the row asked for, and what happened\n\n**Arm 1 — the cross-family round.** Drawn on trunk `2f660cb7` via `OPENAI-SOL` (gpt-5.6-sol), hostile read-only brief that named the four rows and told the reviewer nothing about what had moved. **`VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=2`** — it did *not* confirm the rows.\n\n- `TC-199`/`TC-200` **stand**, no finding: seven evidence nodes pass, `verifies` names the LLR arm, TC-176 shared-node claim exact.\n- `LLR-203`/`LLR-204` **did not stand.** WI-543 had shipped the file-to-requirement join, an independent physical-tree universe, a mechanically-parsed exclusion carrier and a four-class warn-to-gate checker — and both Approved rows still asserted none of them existed. Falsified by driving, not reading: `--mapping-purpose` reports `unresolved_reference — 0` over 21 filled references; `delivery_inventory()` walks 213 physical sources; the installer is row 19 of `mapping-source-exclusions`.\n\nI formed that reading first and the round corroborated it independently. Every anchor re-verified before acceptance, including one imprecision in the reviewer's finding 1 — recorded in the round file rather than dropped.\n\n**What I corrected, and what I deliberately did not.** The false sentences (plus a title and a rationale that carried the same premise — half-correcting would have been worse than either) were amended in-lane with `Status` untouched at `Approved`. The design half — which row owns the delivered checker, whether `code_symbol` widens, where TC-204 binds — needs the whole chain a work item doesn't hold, so I left it and stated it as the row's new NOT-DISCHARGED gap. It is not on no queue: I drove `staged_spine_amendments` to confirm the amendment adjudication minted at merge really does list both rows.\n\n**Arm 2 — the two routed BLOCKERs: annotate, no successor.** Both re-verified first (brief and returns are both added by `64e9bf2a`, so the pre-registration claim is unevidenced). Refused a sterile re-run on three grounds — it cannot repair the immutability defect at all, no spine row cites the exercise, and the alignment pass already declines to defer to either return.\n\n**No snapshot write, no `Status` flip** — verified `lane_approval_refusal` returns `None` and `docs/archive/last_approved/` has zero files in the delta.\n\n## One red, and it is mine\n\nFull suite: **`1 failed, 3281 passed, 25 skipped in 576.93s`**. `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` fails. I nearly wrote this off as the known trunk red my notes describe — instead I ran the node at the integration base in a detached worktree and **it passes there**, so this lane caused it.\n\nBenign and the trunk lane's to clear: `low-level-requirements.toml` is a declared derivation input, so amending a cell moves `docs/stage`'s input hash by construction, while the derived values (`per-phase`, `drafted = 9`) are unchanged. I did not restamp `docs/stage` — a work branch may not write a generated artifact, and `trunk_step`'s `derived-stage` regenerates it after merge, which is why the branch-aware bar prints `SKIP derived-stage`. The node is in `SLOW_MODULES`, so the smoke commit bars never saw it; those greens were honest for what they measure.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging to whoever merges: amending two Approved rows is heavier than the literal \"draw a round\" the spec named. I judged it in scope because the row is the WI-508 spine *reseal* and closing with a live falsehood on the approved spine would recreate exactly the \"left on no queue\" defect it exists to fix — but the merge-time adjudication may reasonably want to re-scope that."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1514,"cache_read_input_tokens":225361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1514},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f485ca-7d86-46c9-85e6-54376a8c7e94","uuid":"46a91758-5e55-496a-ac29-c357c955bd28","request_id":"req_011CeeaZaBKAQcc3QHt1tGsX"}
